[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   Step 074 -- leave-one-channel-out robustness of the joint axis test.
[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   Step 069's global result could in principle be driven by a single
[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   strong channel.  Each channel is dropped in turn and the combined
[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   statistic S_-j = -2 sum_{i != j} ln p_i is re-evaluated at the observed
[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   axis against the same 20,000-direction axis-permutation null (same
[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   seed, same draws).  If the joint anomaly remains significant under
[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   every leave-one-out set, no single channel manufactures the result;
[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   the channel whose removal most degrades S is identified as the
[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   largest contributor -- a weight statement, not a significance claim.
[2026-09-20 11:36:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 074]   Inputs : same data stack as step_069
